#: ../content/communication-notifications/postmaster-filters.rst:88
msgid "Filter Condition"
msgstr ""

#: ../content/communication-notifications/postmaster-filters.rst:93
msgid "Postmaster Filter Settings - Filter Condition"
msgstr ""

#: ../content/communication-notifications/postmaster-filters.rst:95
msgid "A postmaster filter consists of one or more conditions that must be met in order for the defined actions to be executed on the email. Filter conditions can be defined for specific mail header entries or for strings in the mail body."
msgstr ""

#: ../content/communication-notifications/postmaster-filters.rst:179
msgid "Search header field … for value"
msgstr ""

#: ../content/communication-notifications/postmaster-filters.rst:98
msgid "Select a mail header or an ``X-OTOBO`` header from the first drop-down list, and enter a value as search term for the selected mail header to the second field. Even regular expressions can be used for extended pattern matching."
msgstr ""

#: ../content/communication-notifications/postmaster-filters.rst:100
msgid "A list of mail header entries can be found in `RFC5322 <https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc5322>`_. It is also possible to define ``X-OTOBO`` headers as filter condition. The different ``X-OTOBO`` headers and their meaning are the following:"
msgstr ""

#: ../content/communication-notifications/postmaster-filters.rst:103
msgid "``X-OTOBO-AttachmentCount``"
msgstr ""

#: ../content/communication-notifications/postmaster-filters.rst:103
msgid "This contains as value the number of attachments which are contained in the email (e.g. *0* for mails without attachments)."
msgstr ""

#: ../content/communication-notifications/postmaster-filters.rst:106
msgid "``X-OTOBO-AttachmentExists``"
msgstr ""

#: ../content/communication-notifications/postmaster-filters.rst:106
msgid "Depending on whether attachments are included in the email this ``X-OTOBO`` header is set to ``yes``, or it has a ``no`` value if no attachments are included."
msgstr ""

#: ../content/communication-notifications/postmaster-filters.rst:109
msgid "``X-OTOBO-BodyDecrypted``"
msgstr ""

#: ../content/communication-notifications/postmaster-filters.rst:109
msgid "If the incoming mail was encrypted, it is possible to add a search term to look for the body of the incoming encrypted mail."
msgstr ""

#: ../content/communication-notifications/postmaster-filters.rst:112
msgid "``X-OTOBO-CustomerNo``"
msgstr ""

#: ../content/communication-notifications/postmaster-filters.rst:112
msgid "Set the customer ID for the ticket."
msgstr ""

#: ../content/communication-notifications/postmaster-filters.rst:115
msgid "``X-OTOBO-CustomerUser``"
msgstr ""

#: ../content/communication-notifications/postmaster-filters.rst:115
msgid "Set the customer user for the ticket."
msgstr ""

#: ../content/communication-notifications/postmaster-filters.rst:118
msgid "``X-OTOBO-DynamicField-<DynamicFieldName>``"
msgstr ""

#: ../content/communication-notifications/postmaster-filters.rst:118
msgid "Saves an additional information value for the ticket on *<DynamicFieldName>* dynamic field. The possible values depend on dynamic field configuration (e.g. text: *Notebook*, date: *2010-11-20 00:00:00*, integer: *1*)."
msgstr ""

#: ../content/communication-notifications/postmaster-filters.rst:121
msgid "``X-OTOBO-FollowUp-*``"
msgstr ""

#: ../content/communication-notifications/postmaster-filters.rst:121
msgid "These headers are the same as the ones without the ``FollowUp`` prefix, but these headers are applied only for follow-up mails."
msgstr ""

#: ../content/communication-notifications/postmaster-filters.rst:124
msgid "``X-OTOBO-FollowUp-State-Keep``"
msgstr ""

#: ../content/communication-notifications/postmaster-filters.rst:124
msgid "If set to *1*, the incoming follow-up message will not change the ticket state. For this purpose the header can be customized in the system configuration using option ``KeepStateHeader``."
msgstr ""

#: ../content/communication-notifications/postmaster-filters.rst:127
msgid "``X-OTOBO-Ignore``"
msgstr ""

#: ../content/communication-notifications/postmaster-filters.rst:127
msgid "If set to ``Yes`` or ``True``, the incoming message will completely be ignored and never delivered to the system."
msgstr ""

#: ../content/communication-notifications/postmaster-filters.rst:130
msgid "``X-OTOBO-IsVisibleForCustomer``"
msgstr ""

#: ../content/communication-notifications/postmaster-filters.rst:130
msgid "Controls if the article is shown to customer users. Possible values are *0* or *1*."
msgstr ""

#: ../content/communication-notifications/postmaster-filters.rst:133
msgid "``X-OTOBO-Lock``"
msgstr ""

#: ../content/communication-notifications/postmaster-filters.rst:133
msgid "Set the lock state of a ticket. Possible values are ``locked`` or ``unlocked``."
msgstr ""

#: ../content/communication-notifications/postmaster-filters.rst:136
msgid "``X-OTOBO-Loop``"
msgstr ""

#: ../content/communication-notifications/postmaster-filters.rst:136
msgid "If set to ``Yes`` or ``True``, no auto answer is delivered to the sender of the message (mail loop protection)."
msgstr ""

#: ../content/communication-notifications/postmaster-filters.rst:139
msgid "``X-OTOBO-Owner``"
msgstr ""

#: ../content/communication-notifications/postmaster-filters.rst:139
msgid "Set the agent as owner for the ticket."
msgstr ""

#: ../content/communication-notifications/postmaster-filters.rst:142
msgid "``X-OTOBO-OwnerID``"
msgstr ""

#: ../content/communication-notifications/postmaster-filters.rst:142
msgid "Set the agent ID as owner for the ticket."
msgstr ""

#: ../content/communication-notifications/postmaster-filters.rst:145
msgid "``X-OTOBO-Priority``"
msgstr ""

#: ../content/communication-notifications/postmaster-filters.rst:145
msgid "Set the priority for the ticket."
msgstr ""

#: ../content/communication-notifications/postmaster-filters.rst:148
msgid "``X-OTOBO-Queue``"
msgstr ""

#: ../content/communication-notifications/postmaster-filters.rst:148
msgid "Set the queue where the ticket shall be sorted. If this is set, all other filter rules that try to sort a ticket into a specific queue are ignored. If you use a sub-queue, specify it as *Parent::Sub*."
msgstr ""

#: ../content/communication-notifications/postmaster-filters.rst:151
msgid "``X-OTOBO-Responsible``"
msgstr ""

#: ../content/communication-notifications/postmaster-filters.rst:151
msgid "Set the agent as responsible for the ticket."
msgstr ""

#: ../content/communication-notifications/postmaster-filters.rst:154
msgid "``X-OTOBO-ResponsibleID``"
msgstr ""

#: ../content/communication-notifications/postmaster-filters.rst:154
msgid "Set the agent ID as responsible for the ticket."
msgstr ""

#: ../content/communication-notifications/postmaster-filters.rst:157
msgid "``X-OTOBO-SenderType``"
msgstr ""

#: ../content/communication-notifications/postmaster-filters.rst:157
msgid "Set the sender type for the ticket. Possible values are ``agent``, ``system`` or ``customer``."
msgstr ""

#: ../content/communication-notifications/postmaster-filters.rst:160
