msgstr ""

#: ../content/processes-automation/web-services.rst:4
msgid "In a connected world, a ticket system needs to be able to react to requests from other systems and also to send requests or information to other systems:"
msgstr ""

#: ../content/processes-automation/web-services.rst:6
msgid "CRM systems"
msgstr ""

#: ../content/processes-automation/web-services.rst:7
msgid "Project management systems"
msgstr ""

#: ../content/processes-automation/web-services.rst:8
msgid "Documentation management systems"
msgstr ""

#: ../content/processes-automation/web-services.rst:9
msgid "and many more"
msgstr ""

#: ../content/processes-automation/web-services.rst:11
msgid "The ticket system must be reachable by other services without manual intervention by an agent."
msgstr ""

#: ../content/processes-automation/web-services.rst:13
msgid "OTOBO supports this requirement by the *Generic Interface*. It empowers the administrator to create a web service for a specific task without scripting language knowledge. OTOBO reacts on incoming REST or SOAP requests and creates objects or provides object data to other systems transparently."
msgstr ""

#: ../content/processes-automation/web-services.rst:15
msgid "A web service is a communication method between two systems, in our case OTOBO and a remote system. In its configuration, the :term:`operation` or :term:`invoker` determine the direction of communication, and the :term:`mapping` and :term:`transport` take care of how the data is received and interpreted."
msgstr ""

#: ../content/processes-automation/web-services.rst:17
msgid "By configuration, you can define what actions the web service can perform internally (operation), what actions the OTOBO request can perform on a remote system (invokers), how data is converted from one system to the other (mapping), and which protocol is used for communication (transport)."
msgstr ""

#: ../content/processes-automation/web-services.rst:19
msgid "The generic interface is the framework which makes it possible to create web services for OTOBO in a predefined way, using ready-made building blocks that are independent from each other and interchangeable."
msgstr ""

